module engine where

-- derive-functor — the generic, schema-directed `fmap` (the kinds-arc capstone,
-- unified-static-analysis Phase 6b).
--
-- Any `* -> *` type WITHOUT an authored `Functor` instance gets `fmap` for FREE:
-- a single always-on structural `Functor` instance keyed by
-- `{$pattern:"engine:isUnaryConstructor"}` resolves through the SHIPPED
-- `matchStructural` substrate (6a made real parametric constructors dispatch by
-- KIND), and its `fmap` is `engine:deriveFmap` — a thin category-B
-- reflection+marshal bridge (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts) that resolves the
-- dispatched value's owning type, marshals its schema across the `$`-key barrier
-- via `marshalTraversalType`, and delegates the DECISION to THIS body. The
-- authored `Maybe`/`List`/`Result` instances keep nominal precedence
-- (`resolveStructural` is the last fall-through), so this only fires for
-- previously-uninstanced unary constructors (e.g. a user `Box a` / `Tree a`).
--
-- This is the `$tag`-correct, multi-param-SOUND Fenel successor to the stale
-- `__case`-era TS `structuralMap` (engine/src/structural.ts) it RETIRES: it
-- classifies fields by the FUNCTOR-PARAM IDENTITY (`TtVar paramName`), recurses
-- on self-recursive fields (`TtNamed typeName`), and LEAVES every other field —
-- where `structuralMap` mapped EVERY non-recursive field (wrong for `Result`'s
-- `e`, `Pair2 e a`'s `e`, …). The schema is the dispatched type AS A RUNTIME
-- VALUE (runtime reflection over types) — the `types = UI = app` payoff.
--
-- TOTALITY (D-6b-4): the recursion descends ONLY into self-recursive sub-values
-- (`fieldVal` is a structural sub-term of `value`), strictly smaller each step;
-- an unknown tag / non-record value / unrecognised field-type ⇒ LEAVE (never
-- crash). The fold is its own dog-food for the totality checker this workstream
-- builds.
--
-- NESTED FOREIGN FUNCTOR (D-6b-5, CLOSED in 6c): a field where the param sits
-- DIRECTLY under a DIFFERENT constructor (`Maybe a` / `List a` inside another
-- functor; marshalled `TtApp` whose args carry `TtVar paramName`, NOT a bare
-- `TtVar` and NOT self-recursive) is now MAPPED by RE-DISPATCHING `Functor.fmap
-- g fieldVal` — the nested functor resolves its OWN instance (nominal for
-- `List`/`Maybe`, derived for a user functor). Re-entrancy is safe: the nested
-- type differs from the outer (a same-type field is the self-recursive case),
-- so `resolveStructural`'s `(class,type)` fence is never tripped on the same key.
-- FENCE (D-6c-2): COMPOUND nesting two functors deep (`List (Box a)` ⇒ the
-- inner `TtApp` arg is itself a `TtApp`, not a bare `TtVar paramName`) needs
-- `fmap (fmap g)` composition — still LEFT, documented, never silently partial.
-- An APPLIED self-reference (`Tree a` ⇒ `TtApp`) is recognised as the
-- self-recursive `TtNamed` case where the encoding gives it (the `structuralView`
-- precedent).
--
-- `$map`-FIELD DESCENT (D-6c-3 CLOSED, array-substrate Phase 1a). A `TtMap` field
-- whose VALUES carry the functor param directly (`Map String a`, marshalled
-- `TtMap { values = TtVar paramName }`) is now MAPPED by calling `mapFmap g` on
-- the field value — the `Functor (Map k)` operation (algebra-methods.fenel),
-- which maps the map's values keys-fixed. A direct call, NOT a `Functor.fmap`
-- re-dispatch: a bare map field value carries no `$tag`, so it has no reflectable
-- type identity to dispatch on (the Phase-1a Step-0 fact — runtime dispatch keys
-- on `typeConstructorOf`), but the `mapFmap` body operates on the bare-object
-- entries directly. COMPOUND map values (`Map String (Box a)` ⇒ values is a
-- `TtApp`, not a bare `TtVar paramName`) stay LEFT (the D-6c-2 compound fence,
-- same as a compound `TtApp` arg).
--
-- The marshalled `TraversalType` ADT is declared in type-traversal.fenel
-- (TtVariant / TtRecord / TtOpaque / TtMu / TtVar / TtNamed / TtField /
-- TtVariantCase / …); this body pattern-matches it the way type-traversal.fenel
-- + type-subsumes.fenel do. All helpers are prefixed `deriveFmap…` to avoid
-- registry collisions. std fns (`mapGet`/`assocRecord`/`eq`/`head`/`tail`) are
-- called by bare codeName (the engine-body idiom); the continuation `g` is a
-- closure-valued PARAM applied via `$` (low-precedence application — bare `g x`
-- would parse as a call-by-NAME fnId, the algebra-methods.fenel convention).

-- deriveFmapFold — the entry. `g` the function, `value` the runtime functor
-- value, `schemaView` the dispatched type's schema marshalled to TraversalType,
-- `paramName` the functor type-param name (the type's LAST declared param, by the
-- `f<a>` convention), `typeName` the owning type-constructor name (for
-- self-recursion detection). Peels the schema wrappers to the variant/record,
-- finds the matching case, rebuilds it. The 5th `typeName` arg is the build-time
-- amendment to the brief's 4-arg sketch — self-recursion is `TtNamed typeName`,
-- so the body needs the name (the bridge supplies it).
@label "Derive fmap (generic fold)"
@description "Phase 6b — the generic schema-directed `fmap`: any `* -> *` type without an authored Functor instance gets fmap free. Maps the functor-param leaves (TtVar paramName), recurses self-recursive fields (TtNamed typeName), leaves the rest (multi-param sound, the structuralMap repair). The decision half of the derived Functor instance; the engine:deriveFmap bridge supplies (g, value, schemaView, paramName, typeName). Total: descends only into strictly-smaller self-recursive sub-values."
@tags "engine" "functor" "derive" "kinds" "phase-6b"
deriveFmapFold : (g: a) -> (value: b) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFmapFold g value schemaView paramName typeName =
  case schemaView of
    TtOpaque { pure = p } -> deriveFmapFold g value p paramName typeName
    TtRefined { base = bse } -> deriveFmapFold g value bse paramName typeName
    TtMu { body = bdy } -> deriveFmapFold g value bdy paramName typeName
    TtRecord { fields = fs } ->
      deriveFmapRebuild g value fs schemaView paramName typeName
    TtVariant { cases = cs } ->
      case mapGet value "$tag" of
        Nothing -> value
        Just tag ->
          case deriveFmapFindCase cs tag of
            Nothing -> value
            Just c -> deriveFmapRebuild g value c.fields schemaView paramName typeName
    _ -> value

-- deriveFmapFindCase — locate the variant case whose name matches the value's
-- `$tag`. Internal helper; head/tail recursion (the array-repr List idiom).
@label "derive-functor: findCase"
@description "Phase 6b — locate the TtVariantCase matching the value's $tag. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6b"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapFindCase : (cases: List a) -> (tag: String) -> Maybe a
deriveFmapFindCase cases tag =
  case head cases of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just c ->
      if eq c.name tag
        then Just c
        else case tail cases of
          Nothing -> Nothing
          Just rest -> deriveFmapFindCase rest tag

-- deriveFmapRebuild — thread the accumulator FROM `value` so `$tag` + every
-- untouched field are preserved automatically (assocRecord = `{...rec, [k]:v}`);
-- per declared field, set the (re)mapped value. Internal helper.
@label "derive-functor: rebuild"
@description "Phase 6b — rebuild a case's value: thread acc from value (preserves $tag + untouched fields), set each declared field to its mapped value. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6b"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapRebuild : (g: a) -> (value: b) -> (fields: List c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFmapRebuild g value fields schemaView paramName typeName =
  deriveFmapRebuildGo g value value fields schemaView paramName typeName

-- deriveFmapRebuildGo — the accumulator-threaded fold behind rebuild.
@label "derive-functor: rebuildGo"
@description "Phase 6b — accumulator-threaded fold: walk the declared fields, assoc each mapped value onto the accumulator. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6b"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapRebuildGo : (g: a) -> (acc: b) -> (value: b) -> (fields: List c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFmapRebuildGo g acc value fields schemaView paramName typeName =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just f ->
      let acc2 = deriveFmapStepField g acc value f schemaView paramName typeName
      case tail fields of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> deriveFmapRebuildGo g acc2 value rest schemaView paramName typeName

-- deriveFmapStepField — one field step. A field absent from the value (a partial
-- record) is LEFT untouched (no assoc); else assoc the classified+mapped value.
-- Split out to avoid a `case`-in-`let` (the analyze.fenel/totality.fenel idiom).
@label "derive-functor: stepField"
@description "Phase 6b — one field: read the value's field (absent ⇒ leave acc untouched), classify+map, assoc onto acc. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6b"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapStepField : (g: a) -> (acc: b) -> (value: b) -> (f: c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> b
deriveFmapStepField g acc value f schemaView paramName typeName =
  case mapGet value f.name of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just fieldVal ->
      assocRecord acc f.name (deriveFmapMapField g fieldVal f.type schemaView paramName typeName)

-- deriveFmapMapField — CLASSIFY one field by its marshalled TraversalType:
--   element       — `TtVar paramName`   ⇒ apply the continuation `g`.
--   self-recursive — `TtNamed typeName` ⇒ recurse `deriveFmapFold` (same schema).
--   map-field      — `TtMap` whose values carry the param ⇒ `mapFmap g` over the
--                    map's values (D-6c-3, closed Phase 1a — a direct call, the
--                    bare map field has no `$tag` to re-dispatch on).
--   otherwise (a different type-var `e`, a fixed `Int`, an unrelated named type,
--             a compound-nested `TtApp`/`TtMap`) ⇒ LEAVE unchanged.
-- D-6b-1: classification is by FUNCTOR-PARAM IDENTITY, not "non-recursive" — the
-- multi-param soundness repair over the legacy `structuralMap`. The `TtApp` case
-- (6c) closes D-6b-5: a one-level nested foreign functor re-dispatches `fmap`.
@label "derive-functor: mapField"
@description "Phase 6b/6c/1a — classify a field by its TraversalType: TtVar paramName ⇒ apply g (the functor param); TtNamed typeName ⇒ recurse (self-recursive); TtApp carrying the param ⇒ re-dispatch Functor.fmap on the nested functor value (D-6b-5, one level, 6c); TtMap whose values carry the param ⇒ mapFmap g over the map values (D-6c-3, closed Phase 1a); else leave (other vars / fixed types / compound nesting). Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6b"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapMapField : (g: a) -> (fieldVal: d) -> (ft: TraversalType) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> d
deriveFmapMapField g fieldVal ft schemaView paramName typeName =
  case ft of
    TtVar { name = vn } ->
      if eq vn paramName
        then (g $ fieldVal)
        else fieldVal
    TtNamed { name = nn } ->
      if eq nn typeName
        then deriveFmapFold g fieldVal schemaView paramName typeName
        else fieldVal
    TtApp { args = as } ->
      if deriveFmapAppHasParam as paramName
        then fmap g fieldVal
        else fieldVal
    TtMap { values = vs } ->
      if deriveFmapArgIsParam vs paramName
        then mapFmap g fieldVal
        else fieldVal
    _ -> fieldVal

-- deriveFmapAppHasParam — does this applied-type's arg list carry the functor
-- param DIRECTLY as one of its args (`Con .. a ..`)? Only a bare `TtVar
-- paramName` counts — a nested `TtApp` arg (compound nesting, `List (Box a)`)
-- does NOT, so it falls to the LEAVE branch (D-6c-2 fence). Internal helper;
-- head/tail recursion. (Sibling of derive-foldable.fenel's deriveFoldrAppHasParam
-- — kept per-file to keep the two derivation modules independent.)
@label "derive-functor: appHasParam"
@description "Phase 6c — does an applied-type's arg list carry the functor param directly (one-level nesting)? A nested TtApp arg (compound nesting) does NOT count — D-6c-2 fence. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapAppHasParam : (args: List a) -> (paramName: String) -> Bool
deriveFmapAppHasParam args paramName =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> false
    Just a ->
      if deriveFmapArgIsParam a paramName
        then true
        else case tail args of
          Nothing -> false
          Just rest -> deriveFmapAppHasParam rest paramName

-- deriveFmapArgIsParam — is this single TraversalType arg the functor param
-- (`TtVar paramName`)? Internal helper.
@label "derive-functor: argIsParam"
@description "Phase 6c — is a single TraversalType arg the functor param (TtVar paramName)? Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "functor" "phase-6c"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveFmapArgIsParam : (a: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> Bool
deriveFmapArgIsParam a paramName =
  case a of
    TtVar { name = vn } -> eq vn paramName
    _ -> false
